    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0155" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg85"/>

                <head>No. 39.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Logan
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 13, 1882</date>.
                        (Received January 16, 1883.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon the failure to undertake the voyage to
                    Arequipa with Señor Calderon, as recorded in my dispatch No. 26, I determined to
                    address an unofficial communication upon the existing situation to Vice
                    President Montero. A copy of this document is inclosed under cover of this
                    dispatch.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. A. LOGAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d39-a1.xml" xpointer="d39-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
